Demonstrate specimen, microscope, and analytical-observation competence (@mp-lab-project: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mineralogy-and-petrology, #source "../sources/Mineralogy-and-Optical-Laboratory-Manual.lingua#r_4EH79TNHB2YMYGY79B5PV11FTG", #source "../sources/Optical-Mineralogy-Brock.lingua#r_4HWN93T5EATAS40HNJGMCHSM7E", #source "../sources/Guide-to-Thin-Section-Microscopy.lingua#r_2MH30T4MGW8YMVP9SA3Z7XCDSD", #source "../sources/Virtual-Petrography-Toronto.lingua#r_4ZA3K3DY6FMKNN06EFJ8X8SARS", #mineralogy-and-petrology "Integrated-crystal-and-analytical-characterization.lingua#r_5C4Q9327N8YT8SAN6Q8F2SJF1P") { r_32GJMXG5AZ5WT3PCQHY77G2WB0
**Read:** [Mineralogy and Optical Mineralogy Laboratory Manual — McNamee and Gunter](../sources/Mineralogy-and-Optical-Laboratory-Manual.lingua#r_4EH79TNHB2YMYGY79B5PV11FTG), the complete manual and final projects; [Optical Mineralogy — Brock University course and laboratory material](../sources/Optical-Mineralogy-Brock.lingua#r_4HWN93T5EATAS40HNJGMCHSM7E), the complete public laboratory sequence; [Guide to Thin Section Microscopy — Raith, Raase, and Reinhardt](../sources/Guide-to-Thin-Section-Microscopy.lingua#r_2MH30T4MGW8YMVP9SA3Z7XCDSD), the entire guide with all relevant procedures; [Virtual Petrography — Daxberger and Kennedy, University of Toronto Scarborough](../sources/Virtual-Petrography-Toronto.lingua#r_4ZA3K3DY6FMKNN06EFJ8X8SARS), selected identified practice specimens.

Work a substantial known/unknown teaching collection with appropriate supervision, instruments, reference specimens, and preparation. Complete the mineralogy/optical manual's full sequence and projects and the Brock labs. Use the practical guide's complete adjustment and measurement procedures, preserving actual sample and method identities.

Describe hand specimens and thin sections through physical, plane-light, crossed-light, and suitable conoscopic observations, including unfavorable orientations, alteration, fine mixtures, and ambiguous candidates. Explain identification with convergent properties and state where exact species/composition needs additional analysis.

Perform calibrated length/angle/thickness or relative-index work as appropriate and compare independent repetitions/known material. Distinguish actual variability, preparation effects, instrument limitations, and observer classification. A specimen collection identified by copied labels does not demonstrate the method.

**Work:** produce original descriptions, drawings/images with observation conditions, classification arguments, uncertainty, and a revised account after independent critique. Complete a quantitative mode or domain measurement with a justified sampling design. For an unknown, identify the most useful next analytical test and explain what alternative it discriminates.

Virtual sections and published datasets can prepare recognition and reasoning; state their demonstrated scope. Full practical claims require actual appropriate specimen/instrument work. No private instructor answer collection or new Lince assessment infrastructure is assumed.

**Continue:** [Characterize a material by independent structural, optical, and chemical evidence](Integrated-crystal-and-analytical-characterization.lingua#r_5C4Q9327N8YT8SAN6Q8F2SJF1P).

**Return:** [Mineralogy and petrology — minerals, crystals, rock processes, and investigation](../Mineralogy-and-petrology.lingua#r_44F7X6GPMW6ZSCCN6D71QSVKBN).
